# No Em or En Dashes

Do not use em dashes (— U+2014) or en dashes (– U+2013) in any output: chat replies, rules, docs, comments, UI copy, commits, or code strings.

## Use instead

- Plain ASCII hyphen-minus: `-` (U+002D) for ranges, compounds, and parenthetical breaks
- Or another explicit UTF-8 character the user asks for (e.g. `~`, `/`, `|`) when a hyphen is wrong for the meaning

## Examples

```text
BAD: Improve SEO — then ship
GOOD: Improve SEO - then ship

BAD: pages 12–15
GOOD: pages 12-15

BAD: React–Vite stack
GOOD: React-Vite stack
```

## Checklist

- Before finishing a file or reply, scan for `—` and `–` and replace with `-` (or the agreed alternative)
- Do not paste prose that reintroduces em/en dashes from external sources without converting them
